{"id":"the-recipe-for-clockwise-siteswaps","name":"The recipe for clockwise siteswaps","chapter":"Six handed siteswaps","kind":"guide","page":115,"label":"114","jugglers":3,"objects":null,"timing":null,"pdf":"book/highgate.pdf#page=115&view=FitH,779","passist":null,"passist_candidate":null,"passist_fork":null,"notations":[{"type":"hg-siteswap-in-text","value":"ab9b9a3b9a6ab96"},{"type":"hg-siteswap-in-text","value":"453534"},{"type":"hg-siteswap-in-text","value":"353404530"},{"type":"hg-siteswap-in-text","value":"ab9b9a3b9a6ab96"},{"type":"hg-siteswap-in-text","value":"b9aab939abb6a69"},{"type":"hg-siteswap-in-text","value":"ab9b9a3b9a6ab96"}],"derived":{"kind":"local-6hss","global":"ab9b9a3b9a6ab96","confidence":"low","matches_stated":null,"per_juggler":{"A":"b9b69","B":"ab3ab","C":"9a9a6"}},"body":[{"t":"p","h":"The recipe for clockwise six handed siteswaps is essentially the same as for anticlockwise six handed siteswaps. The difference is that the causal diagram is flipped upside down. As a result the beats are numbered clockwise around the triangle of jugglers."},{"t":"li","h":"Take any siteswap. I&#x27;m going to choose the nine object pattern ab9b9a3b9a6ab96."},{"t":"li","h":"Subtract 6 from every number to give a derived siteswap. In my example the derived"},{"t":"p","h":"siteswap is 453534-353404530. (Despite the negative numbers, this is still a siteswap)!"},{"t":"li","h":"Number the beats in a causal diagram as follows:"},{"t":"d","i":0},{"t":"li","h":"Use the derived siteswap to complete the causal diagram:"},{"t":"d","i":1},{"t":"p","h":"Ben feeds on Martin&#x27;s one count. His pattern is Anne Clare zip Anne Clare. Ben throws crossing passes to Anne and straight passes to Clare. Clare and Anne pass to Ben on Jim&#x27;s two count. Anne starts left handed, a third of a beat after Ben. Her pattern is pass self pass hold self with crossing passes to Ben. Clare starts two thirds of a beat after Ben. Her pattern is self pass self pass hold with straight passes to Ben."},{"t":"p","h":"If we relabel the beats in Anne&#x27;s pattern then all Ben&#x27;s passes are straight and Anne and Clare throw crossing passes to Ben:"},{"t":"d","i":2},{"t":"p","h":"This pattern is Martin&#x27;s one count feeding Jim&#x27;s two count. The clockwise siteswap for this feed is: ab9b9a3b9a6ab96."},{"t":"p","h":"With six handed siteswap there are two different ways to describe Martin&#x27;s one count feeding Jim&#x27;s two count. The anticlockwise siteswap is: b9aab939abb6a69 and the clockwise siteswap is: ab9b9a3b9a6ab96. What people actually do when they juggle this feed lies somewhere in between."},{"t":"p","h":"One possibility is for Anne and Clare to start half a beat after Ben:"},{"t":"d","i":3},{"t":"p","h":"The alternative is for all three jugglers to start at the same time:"},{"t":"d","i":4},{"t":"p","h":"In this case everyone gets hurried throws instead of holds."},{"t":"p","h":"The following table shows all the throws in six handed siteswap up to height h (17)."},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"hr"},{"t":"hr"}],"drawings":[{"file":"p115-1.png","kind":"causal diagram","reading":{"rows":[{"juggler":"A","name":"Anne","offset":0.3333333333333333,"tempo":1.0,"beats":[{"t":0.3333333333333333,"hand":"L","n":2},{"t":1.3333333333333333,"hand":"R","n":5},{"t":2.3333333333333335,"hand":"L","n":8},{"t":3.3333333333333335,"hand":"R","n":11},{"t":4.333333333333333,"hand":"L","n":14},{"t":5.333333333333333,"hand":"R","n":17},{"t":6.333333333333333,"hand":"L","n":20},{"t":7.333333333333333,"hand":"R","n":23},{"t":8.333333333333334,"hand":"L","n":26},{"t":9.333333333333334,"hand":"R","n":29},{"t":10.333333333333334,"hand":"L"}]},{"juggler":"B","name":"Ben","offset":0.0,"tempo":1.0,"beats":[{"t":0.0,"hand":"R","n":1},{"t":1.0,"hand":"L","n":4},{"t":2.0,"hand":"R","n":7},{"t":3.0,"hand":"L","n":10},{"t":4.0,"hand":"R","n":13},{"t":5.0,"hand":"L","n":16},{"t":6.0,"hand":"R","n":19},{"t":7.0,"hand":"L","n":22},{"t":8.0,"ha